New procedure:
use /home/common/SAN/CreateASM.sh

=====================================

1. Scan hba's for new storage. 
2. multipath
3. fdisk /dev/mapper/mpath[?] { n, p, 1, <enter>, <enter>, x, b, 128} 
4. On RHEL6: partprobe /dev/mapper/mpath[?]
   On RHEL5: kpartx -av /dev/mapper/mpath[?]
   Make sure /dev/mpath/mpath[?]p1 and /dec/mapper/mpath[?]p1 exist
5 /etc/init.d/oracleasm createdisk DATA## /dev/mapper/mpath?p1
On second server:
6. Scan hba's for new storage
7. multipath
9. /etc/init.d/oracleasm scandisks

***
If the createdisk command hangs for more than 30 seconds, 
run the following command (per Redhat) to check on status:
dmsetup info -c 
If you see a "S" then it's Suspended.
Run the following to Resume the LUN:
dmsetup resume mpathXXp1 (replace XX with your actual LUN #)
Queued commands should finish successfully now.
***